I finish the mawa cake.
I drink the last sip of tea.
I like this cafe very much.
But now I have to go home.
I look at the waiter.
I raise my hand.
"Bhaiya, listen!" I say.
He comes near my table.
"Yes madam?" he asks.
"I am done eating," I smile.
"I need the bill."
"Will you give the bill?" I ask.
"Yes madam, one minute," he says.
He goes towards the counter.
I take my wallet out from my bag.
He comes back quickly.
He puts a small slip on the table.
"Thank you bhaiya," I say.
I pick up the slip.
